um_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Rule 12d1-4 requirements beyond statutory limits (management investment companies)**\n\n**Acquiring fund's adviser** must:\n- Evaluate the complexity of the fund-of-funds structure and its aggregate fees and expenses.\n- Find that the acquiring fund's fees and expenses do not duplicate those of the acquired fund.\n- Report these evaluations and findings to the acquiring fund's board.\n\n**Acquired fund's adviser** must:\n- Find that any undue-influence concerns from the investment are reasonably addressed.\n- Report this to the acquired fund's board.\n- Generally not required for secondary-market purchases of listed shares.\n\n**Fund-of-funds investment agreement**\n- Required when the funds have different advisers (or advisers that are not control affiliates).\n- Must be in effect at the time of investment.\n- Must include any material terms needed for the advisers' findings.\n- Must allow termination on no more than 60 days' notice.\n- Must require the acquired fund to provide fee and expense information.\n\n**Related conditions**\n- Control and voting limits, including pass-through or mirror voting above 25% (10% for closed-end funds).\n- Restrictions on three-tier structures.\n- Recordkeeping.","ttft_ms":11262,"type":"result","duration_ms":14789,"uuid":"89f903c1-d6c9-4e8d-bc9a-e4cb24184b21","ttft_stream_ms":545,"time_to_request_ms":61,"first_content_frame_ms":545,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
